esponsible": {"00": "accountable", "01": "liable", "10": "answerable", "11": "in charge"}}, {"and": {"00": "plus", "01": "together with", "10": "along with", "11": "as well as"}}, {"safe": {"00": "secure", "01": "protected", "10": "safe and sound", "11": "unharmed"}}, {"implementation": {"00": "execution", "01": "enactment", "10": "application", "11": "installation"}}], "container": "Nanotechnology, the science of manipulating matter on an atomic and molecular scale, offers numerous benefits. It has revolutionized various fields, including medicine, electronics, and energy production. By creating smaller, more efficient devices, nanotechnology has improved drug delivery systems, enhanced electronic performance, and facilitated renewable energy generation. However, with these benefits come risks. The potential toxicity of nanomaterials, privacy concerns with nanosensors, and the ethical implications of manipulating biology raise legitimate concerns. Additionally, the long-term effects of nanotechnology on the environment and human health remain uncertain. Therefore, while nanotechnology holds immense potential, its benefits must be weighed against its associated risks to ensure a responsible and safe implementation.", "encoded_message": "Nanoscience, the area of altering substances on an atomic and molecular level, presents various advantages. It has redefined diverse sectors, including therapeutics, electrical engineering, and energy generation. By forming tinier, more optimized instruments, nano-engineering has upgraded pharmaceutical distribution mechanisms, boosted tech operation, and simplified sustainable energy creation. However, with these pros come hazards. The possible poisonousness of nanostructures, confidentiality anxieties with nanosensors, and the principled consequences of modifying biotechnology evoke valid considerations. Furthermore, the prolonged impacts of nano-engineering on the environment and human health remain uncertain. Therefore, while nanotechnology holds immense potential, its benefits must be weighed against its associated risks to ensure a responsible and safe implementation.", "encoding_time_report": {"container_generation": 3.84, "secret_key_generation": 105.92}, "decoding_time": 0.00047206878662109375, "decoded_message": "0110101100010100100110101101011100001111000111101001010110010101", "error_message": ""}